# CTRLO-OTHER-PICKERS: Ctrl-O over the help catalog (/help), then one key
# at a time between a Ctrl-O and its return.
# fx closes the full transcript before every frame while this menu is up
# (reconcileBeforeFrameRender, app_render_runtime.zig:1206-1215@481104fd), so
# Ctrl-O over it shows nothing and every key below is the menu's own, as
# without Ctrl-O: `held` is the composer's plane with the menu, C-j and C-k
# move the mark (routePickerControlByte, app_input_runtime.zig:1093-1116),
# Escape closes the menu (resolveEscape, :2765).
# fx's trace log (scope full_transcript) shows each Ctrl-O open the screen
# and the frame close it; `home end` keeps it.
# Then Ctrl-O and C-k, and Ctrl-O and C-j, each pair one `send-keys` of two
# bytes, so one burst: the screen is still up for the second byte, no picker
# takes it (routePickerControlByte, app_input_runtime.zig:1093-1116), and the
# composer does -- a kill of nothing, then a new line in the catalog's
# search (:513-521), which no word of the search is (`burst-ck`, `burst-cj`).
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0 FX_TRACE_LOG=@HOME@/trace.txt FX_TRACE_SCOPES=full_transcript
wait 2
type /help
key Enter
wait 1
snap open
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap held
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Down
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap down
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-k
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap ck
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-j
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap cj
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Tab
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap tab
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Escape
wait 0.8
snap esc
type /help
key Enter
wait 1
key Down
wait 0.5
key -H 0f 0b
wait 0.8
snap burst-ck
key -H 0f 0a
wait 0.8
snap burst-cj
home end
